{0 investing-core}

Retail brokerage as pure values: instruments, end-of-day prices, fractional market
orders, positions with average cost basis, and the ledger entries for the cash side of
each order. Nothing here persists or opens a connection; a service stores the values and
reaches a broker or a data vendor through {!Investing_core.Broker.S} and
{!Investing_core.Market_data.S}.

{1 Where to start}

- {!Investing_core.Placement}: check an order request against the instrument, the latest
  price and the position, and size it.
- {!Investing_core.Order}: the order state machine.
- {!Investing_core.Booking}: the ledger entries for holds, fills and releases.
- {!Investing_core.Position} and {!Investing_core.Portfolio}: holdings, cost basis and
  results.
- {!Investing_core.Price_history} and {!Investing_core.Staleness}: reference prices and
  how old they may be.
- {!Investing_core.Sim_broker} and {!Investing_core.Market_data.Simulated}: everything
  runnable without a broker or a data vendor.
- {!Investing_core.Recurring_buy}: the hook for scheduled buys.

{1 Example}

[examples/quickstart.ml] in the repository takes one buy from simulated closes to a
portfolio summary; [dune test] checks its output.
